ns.WhatsNew = {
    { version = "6.5", text = "|cffffffffRestart the game fully after updating|r (not just /reload): this version adds new files.\n\nBankers and vendors stop making small talk, full bags make room for your loot, and FlareUI now speaks Dutch. Plus a big stack of fixes from your Discord reports.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Language: |cffffffffNederlands|r (Dutch), by LouCryox. Pick it in Settings › Language.\n• Quality of Life › Convenience:\n      - |cffffffffSkip Gossip|r (off): bankers, vendors, trainers, innkeepers and flight masters open their window at once when they have nothing else to say. Hold Shift to talk normally. It never skips in dungeons or raids.\n      - |cffffffffDelete Junk When Full|r (off): with your bags full, clicking an item in the loot window first deletes your cheapest grey item to make room. The chat says what was deleted.\n• Minimap: |cffffffffFlareUI Minimap Button|r (on), above |cffffffffAddon Button Drawer|r.\n      - It shows on the minimap, or in the drawer when the drawer is on.\n      - Right-click the button to hide it. Turn the switch back on to bring it back.\n• Bags & Looting › Item Slots: |cffffffffSkin Item Slots|r (on). Turn it off to keep Blizzard's slots, for example when another addon skins your bags.\n• Bags & Looting › Fonts: |cffffffffItem Level|r, for the item level numbers in your bags and on the character sheet. It shows while |cffffffffItem Level|r is on.\n• Unit frames › Health Text and Power Text:\n      - |cffffffffValue | Percent|r\n      - |cffffffffValue <  > Percent|r (Forever Style only): the value at the bar's left end, the percent at its right end.\n• Bags: pointing at the keyring or crafting bag icon lights up its slots in the backpack.\n• |cffffd100/fui padlog|r: prints the right stick's moves while a controller radial is open, for \"Release the Stick to Use\" reports.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Action bars: with |cffffffffShow Button Art|r off, Action Bar 1 drops its bar art too, as if its |cffffffffHide Bar Art|r were on in Edit Mode.\n• Bags: |cffffffffUpgrade Arrow|r is gone. Its guesses weren't reliable. Addons like Pawn do this properly.\n• Bags & Looting › Item Slots: |cffffffffRarity Colours|r now comes before |cffffffffThicker Borders|r. Both grey out when |cffffffffSkin Item Slots|r is off.\n• Bags: item level numbers use the new |cffffffffItem Level|r font, not |cffffffffBag Items|r. If you had set a Bag Items font, set Item Level too.\n• Unit frames: |cffffffffValue [Max]|r now sits right below |cffffffffValue|r in the Health Text and Power Text lists.\n• French: every phrase added since 6.2 reviewed, and wording made consistent, by Braincell80.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Chat: switching tabs could make the chat disappear until /reload.\n• Chat: separate chat windows no longer show Blizzard's own tab next to FlareUI's.\n• Edit Mode: switching between layouts no longer sends frames back to their default spots. Frames you never moved in one layout keep their spots from the other.\n• Meters › threat window:\n      - It no longer snaps with |cffffffffSnap to Elements|r off.\n      - The arrow keys move it straight, not diagonally.\n      - It stays put after /reload. Your saved spot may shift once after updating.\n• Meters: the meter is styled from the first fight after a reload.\n• FlareUI Style: auras and cast bars draw above the portrait ring and the elite dragon, instead of under them.\n      - Unit frames, boss frames and party frames\n• Spellbook: with |cffffffffKeep Page 1 in Stealth|r, spells on bar 1 no longer glow as if they weren't on your bars.\n• Cooldown Manager: with |cffffffffSkin Cooldown Manager|r on, the Utility icons' border now matches the Essential icons'.\n• Mail Address Book: |cffffffffYour Characters|r fills in the first and last name. Each alt shows its full name after you log in on it once.\n• Unit frames: \"Ghost\" is now translated." },
    { version = "6.4.1", text = "A round of fixes from your reports, plus one small option for poison users.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Buff Reminders › When and Where: |cffffffffOn Mouseover|r is a new |cffffffffWhere|r choice for Class Buffs, Weapon Buffs, Pets and Consumables.\n      - Those icons stay hidden until you point at the reminder row.\n      - They can still be clicked, and they don't play the reminder sound.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Gamepad mode: the chat uses Blizzard's own tabs.\n• Raid frames: with |cffffffffGroups|r set to Columns, |cffffffffGrowth|r is back, as From the Middle, Right or Left.\n• Meters: hovering the meter while it fades holds it in place. Moving away lets the fade finish.\n• Minimap: while OneForAll's |cffffffffCollect minimap buttons|r is on, FlareUI leaves addon buttons on the minimap for it.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Gamepad mode: closing a chat box with Esc no longer breaks the controller.\n• Player cast bar: |cffffffffLatency Zone|r shows each cast's real delay, not the game's slow network average.\n• Action bars: buttons no longer flash as the global cooldown ends on bars with a |cffffffffVisibility|r or a |cffffffffFade Group|r." },
    { version = "6.4", text = "|cffffffffRestart the game fully after updating|r (not just /reload): this version adds a new file.\n\nFonts moved out of Edit Mode and back to the settings panel. Borders can now be turned off entirely, and party and raid frames can sit flush against each other. Every line of settings text got shorter, too.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Borders: |cffffffffNone|r is the first choice in every Border list.\n      - Unit frames, party, raid and boss frames\n      - Cast bars, resource bars and the XP bar\n• XP bar: |cffffffffBorder|r (FlareUI Thin), in its Edit Mode window.\n• Forever Style: every frame off the bronze plate now has Border options.\n      - Simple pet, simple target of target and target of focus\n      - Raid Style party frames and raid frames\n      - Party pet and target frames, and their cast bars\n• Party frames, Raid Style:\n      - |cffffffffPower Text|r (None)\n      - |cffffffffPower Bar for Mana Users Only|r (off)\n      - |cffffffffDispel Icons|r (Middle of the Health Bar) now has a place, like on the raid frames\n      - Three more aura places: |cffffffffInside, Centre|r, |cffffffffInside, Centre Left|r and |cffffffffInside, Centre Right|r\n• Raid frames: |cffffffffAbsorb Texture|r (FlareUI Striped).\n• Target and focus frames: |cffffffffFlip Portrait|r (off), in FlareUI and Forever Style.\n• Meters:\n      - |cffffffffVisibility|r: a new |cffffffffIn an Instance|r choice.\n      - Threat › |cffffffffVisibility|r (With the Meter) for the separate threat window: With the Meter, In an Instance, In a Group or In Combat.\n• |cffffd100/fui saylog|r: checks that every Say and Yell line reaches your chat, and flags any that don't.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Fonts are back on the settings panel, out of Edit Mode.\n      - New |cffffffffFonts|r tabs: Unit Frames, Resource Bars, Buffs & Debuffs, Buff Reminders, Minimap and Quest Tracker.\n      - One section per frame. Every section starts closed.\n      - Each font has its own |cffffffffReset|r, on its heading.\n      - |cffffffffApply to All|r and |cffffffffApply to Both|r are gone. |cffffffffGlobal Font|r gives every font one face.\n      - Your fonts carry over.\n• Party and raid frames: |cffffffffSpacing|r is measured between the bars, so 0 makes them touch.\n      - Raid Style party frames and raid frames, including |cffffffffGroup Spacing|r and the main tank frames.\n      - Your current spacing is adjusted, so your frames stay where they are.\n• Switches that add a part now say |cffffffffShow|r, and are on by default.\n      - Cast bars: |cffffffffShow Icon|r and |cffffffffShow Spell Timer|r\n      - Action bars: |cffffffffShow Keybind Text|r and |cffffffffShow Macro Text|r\n      - Quest Tracker: |cffffffffShow Quest Level|r and |cffffffffShow Completed Objectives|r\n      - Your settings carry over.\n• Edit Mode, unit frames:\n      - |cffffffffMirror|r is now |cffffffffMirror Bars|r.\n      - The |cffffffffAura Ordering|r section is gone. |cffffffffSort By|r sits under Debuffs in Auras; |cffffffffReverse Order|r and |cffffffffYour Auras First|r sit under Only My Buffs / Debuffs.\n      - |cffffffffRange Check|r moved from Look to Frame.\n• Settings text: shorter, plainer descriptions and tips everywhere, in every language.\n• XP bar: rested XP starts after quest XP instead of hiding behind it, and is light blue.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Unit frames: changing |cffffffffAura Timer|r shows or hides the timers at once, not only after a reload.\n• Party frames: |cffffffffReset To Default|r from Raid Style no longer stretches the Classic frames.\n      - Frames already stretched: select them in Classic and press Reset To Default once.\n• Fishing: |cffffffffDouble-Click to Fish|r catches the second click every time.\n• Bags:\n      - The search box fits the window at fewer |cffffffffColumns|r.\n      - With a two-handed weapon, upgrade arrows only compare main-hand and off-hand items.\n      - Closing the backpack with B also closes the reagent bag, so your next bank visit opens your bags." },
